## Implementation Notes

### JSON Extraction

**Problem**: AI might return:
```
Here's the summary:
```json
{"title":"..."}
```
```

**Solution**: Extract first `{` to last `}`:
```typescript
function extractJSON(text: string): string {
  const firstBrace = text.indexOf('{');
  const lastBrace = text.lastIndexOf('}');

  if (firstBrace === -1 || lastBrace === -1) {
    throw new Error('No JSON object found in response');
  }

  return text.substring(firstBrace, lastBrace + 1);
}
```

### Validation Rules

From TYPES-001 AISummary interface:

```typescript
interface AISummary {
  title: string;           // < 50 chars, non-empty
  impact: string;          // non-empty
  keyPoints: [string, string, string];  // exactly 3, all non-empty
  action: string;          // non-empty
}
```

**Validation checks**:
```typescript
if (!summary.title || summary.title.length > 50) {
  throw new ValidationError('Title must be 1-50 characters');
}

if (!Array.isArray(summary.keyPoints) || summary.keyPoints.length !== 3) {
  throw new ValidationError('keyPoints must be array of exactly 3 items');
}

if (summary.keyPoints.some(p => !p || !p.trim())) {
  throw new ValidationError('All keyPoints must be non-empty');
}
```

### Error Handling

**Parse errors**: Log raw JSON string for debugging
```typescript
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(jsonStr);
} catch (err) {
  logger.error('Failed to parse AI response', { raw: jsonStr, error: err });
  throw new Error('AI response is not valid JSON');
}
```

**Validation errors**: Log parsed object for debugging
```typescript
try {
  validateAISummary(summary);
} catch (err) {
  logger.error('AI response failed validation', { summary, error: err });
  throw err;
}
```

## Custom Error Types

```typescript
export class ValidationError extends Error {
  constructor(message: string, public details?: any) {
    super(message);
    this.name = 'ValidationError';
  }
}
```

## Logging Strategy

**Success**: Debug level
```typescript
logger.debug('Parsed AI summary', { title: summary.title });
```

**Failure**: Error level with context
```typescript
logger.error('Failed to parse AI response', {
  raw: jsonString.substring(0, 200), // First 200 chars only
  error: err.message
});
```

